cted web context; and the final specialist answer is returned to the user.\nExplain that architecture when the user asks about it.\nDo not pretend to have performed web research.', 'response': 'TCP and UDP are transport-layer protocols used to send data over networks, but they make different trade-offs:\n\n| Feature | TCP | UDP |\n|---|---|---|\n| Connection | Connection-oriented; establishes a connection first | Connectionless; sends packets directly |\n| Reliability | Guarantees ordered, error-checked delivery and retransmits lost data | No guarantee of delivery, order, or retransmission |\n| Speed | Generally slower because of connection management and error recovery | Faster and lower-latency |\n| Data handling | Byte stream | Individual datagrams |\n| Typical uses | Web pages, file transfers, email, SSH | Video calls, online gaming, DNS, live streaming |\n\n**TCP** is like a tracked, confirmed delivery service: dependable but with some overhead.\n\n**UDP** is like sending postcards: quicker and simpler, but packets may be lost, duplicated, or arrive out of order.\n\nIn practice, use **TCP when correctness matters** and **UDP when speed and low latency matter more than perfect delivery**.', 'tool_calls': []}, 'error': None, 'thinking': ''}
