18:16:17 [INFO   ] arco.core.evaluator: Evaluating ground truth data for CommonKnowledge with this data : {'agent_id': 'CommonKnowledge', 'role': 'You are the common-knowledge and architecture specialist. \nYou have no tools. Answer stable questions from your knowled. \nYou also know this workflow architecture: a routing tool-use agent chooses WebSearch, Summary, or CommonKnowledge; WebSearch can call web_search repeatedly; Summary synthesizes the collected web context; and the final specialist answer is returned to the user.\nExplain that architecture when the user asks about it.\nDo not pretend to have performed web research.', 'message': 'The ARCO workflow uses a routing agent to classify the request and select one path:\n\n- **WebSearch**: chosen when the question requires current information, external sources, or fact-checking. The search agent may run multiple web searches and retrieve relevant pages.\n- **Summary**: used after web searching, once enough results have been collected. It synthesizes those results into a coherent context.\n- **CommonKnowledge**: chosen for stable general-knowledge questions or questions about the workflow’s own architecture, where web research is unnecessary.\n\nFor your question, the router selected **CommonKnowledge** because it asks about the workflow’s decision process itself rather than requesting up-to-date or source-based information.', 'output': {'role': 'You are the common-knowledge and architecture specialist. \nYou have no tools. Answer stable questions from your knowled. \nYou also know this workflow architecture: a routing tool-use agent chooses WebSearch, Summary, or CommonKnowledge; WebSearch can call web_search repeatedly; Summary synthesizes the collected web context; and the final specialist answer is returned to the user.\nExplain that architecture when the user asks about it.\nDo not pretend to have performed web research.', 'response': 'The ARCO workflow uses a routing agent to classify the request and select